ant to find a specific book, you don’t want to walk through every shelf one by one. That would take forever.\n\nInstead, you use a **catalog system**:\n\n1. **The Key**: You know the title of the book you want (e.g., \"Harry Potter\").\n2. **The Hash Function**: You take the title and run it through a special formula (the \"hash\") that turns it into a unique number (e.g., `42`).\n3. **The Bucket**: You go directly to shelf number `42`.\n4. **The Value**: On shelf `42`, you find the book \"Harry Potter\".\n\n**In computer terms:**\n- **Key**: The data you use to look up something (like a username).\n- **Value**: The data you want to retrieve (like the user’s profile).\n- **Hash Map**: A data structure that stores pairs of (Key, Value) so you can find the Value instantly by using the Key.\n\n**Why it’s fast:**\nInstead of checking every item in a list (which takes time proportional to the", "client": {"ttft_s": 0.6158371000055922, "decode_s": 5.481292999997095, "total_s": 6.0975615000061225, "n_gen": 256, "n_chunks": 256, "tg": 46.521869931079245, "pp": 48.71418107114297}}
